rease from £5 044 to £5 664 in 2023. Explain the likely impact of the increase in price of a season ticket on consumer surplus.","topics":["1-2-8-producer-consumer-surplus"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["consumer surplus","price increase","rail fares"],"qpPage":8,"msPage":8,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2023-jun-q4c","p":4,"section":"A","questionNumber":"4(c)","parentQuestion":"4","choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"An annual season ticket for a train journey between London and Reading is planned to increase from £5 044 to £5 664 in 2023. The diagram below shows the demand and supply for sugary drinks. Which one of the following areas represents the change in producer surplus when a minimum price is imposed?","topics":["1-2-8-producer-consumer-surplus","1-4-1-government-intervention-in-markets"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["producer surplus","minimum price","sugary drinks"],"qpPage":9,"msPage":8,"ctxPage":8,"modelAnswer":null,"ctxLabel":"Question 4 as printed","type":"mcq","options":["FEPeP1","FMP1","GEPeP1","GKP1"],"usesFigure":true},{"id":"edexcel-a-p1-2020-oct-q1b","p":8,"section":"A","questionNumber":"1(b)","parentQuestion":"1","choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"Fuel duty is an excise tax imposed on the sale of petrol, included in the price paid by consumers, set at 58 pence per litre. The indirect tax on fuel is increased in a market in which the price elasticity of demand is −0.1. Which one of the following is the most likely effect on consumer and producer surplus?","topics":["1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies","1-2-8-producer-consumer-surplus"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["indirect tax","fuel duty","consumer surplus","producer surplus"],"qpPage":2,"msPage":5,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null,"type":"mcq","options":["Consumer surplus and producer surplus both decrease","Consumer surplus and producer surplus both increase","Consumer surplus decreases and producer surplus increases","Consumer surplus increases and producer surplus decreases"],"usesFigure":false},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2019-jun-q2a","p":30,"section":"A","questionNumber":"2(a)","parentQuestion":"2","choiceGroup":null,"marks":2,"questionText":"The consensus that diesel emissions are bad for health has led to many cities planning to ban diesel vehicles from their centres. The mayors of Paris, Mexico City, Madrid and Athens have said they intend to ban these vehicles by 2025. Annotate the diagram to show the change in consumer surplus in the market for diesel vehicles, following the change in demand caused by the proposed 2025 ban in some city centres.","topics":["1-2-8-producer-consumer-surplus","1-2-2-demand"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["consumer surplus","fall in demand","diesel vehicles","diagram"],"qpPage":4,"msPage":5,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2018-jun-q5a","p":29,"section":"A","questionNumber":"5(a)","parentQuestion":"5","choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"The British Broadcasting Corporation (BBC) is a TV broadcaster. It is financed through an annual TV licence fee of £145.50. At this fee level many TV owners benefit from consumer surplus. Define the term ‘consumer surplus’.","topics":["1-2-8-producer-consumer-surplus"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["consumer surplus","definition"],"qpPage":9,"msPage":8,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-as-p1-2017-jun-q3b","p":28,"section":"A","questionNumber":"3(b)","parentQuestion":"3","choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"In 2015 the UK government cut subsidies for the installation of solar energy panels. The most likely effect of cutting subsidies for the installation of solar panels is to:","topics":["1-2-9-indirect-taxes-subsidies","1-2-8-producer-consumer-surplus"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-1"],"keywords":["subsidy","consumer surplus","solar panels"],"qpPage":5,"msPage":7,"ctxPage":null,"model